Develop a complete bulk acid or alkali supply and receiving investigation (@cs-bulk-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME", #source "../sources/Flammable-Liquid-Tanks-HSE-HSG176.lingua#r_3J96NXWJF945DTPAPBRQPT177R", #source "../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A", #source "../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8", #chemical-supply-systems "A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3") { r_5KQ9YDKC5MCVA114RVMZKH8FT5
**Read:** [Caustic Soda Handbook — OxyChem](../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME), the whole handbook and actual grade/method documents; [Storage of flammable liquids in tanks — HSE HSG176](../sources/Flammable-Liquid-Tanks-HSE-HSG176.lingua#r_3J96NXWJF945DTPAPBRQPT177R), the full applicable guide; [Emissions from Storage — European Commission BREF](../sources/Emissions-from-Storage-BREF.lingua#r_4QFPS62AY03WVQB72BMNJQGC43), complete relevant liquid-storage and transfer chapters; [Water-treatment chemical supply-chain profiles — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chain-Profiles-EPA.lingua#r_0E09Q6T7CC9HNWZB3N84E7K21A), complete chosen chemical profiles; [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), the entire relevant supply-system analysis.

Choose a specific bulk acid or alkali, grade, user and service requirement. Read the entire producer handbook, complete relevant industrial-production chapters, the full applicable tank-storage guide and the relevant EFS chapters. Define the complete chemical and material basis from source to point of use, including impurities, temperature-dependent properties, receiving/working capacity and residual material.

Reconstruct an actual documented chain where evidence is public, separating observed facilities and arrangements from proposed additions. Develop a flowsheet, inventory trajectory, quantity/assay reconciliation, sampling/release method, contact-material account, transport/transfer interface and continuing maintenance/work plan. Use full technical methods and domain-specific qualified review for any physical design or operating proposal.

Compare at least three arrangements, such as direct bulk, terminal/distributor supply and a qualified concentration/conditioning alternative. Examine normal replenishment, delayed release, quality failure and a common utility/transport interruption. Calculate service, resources, losses and dated total cost on one declared basis, with independent arithmetic/model checks and sensitivity.

Submit a substantial reproducible technical study with sources, assumptions, alternative interpretations, uncertainty and an independent critique followed by revision. State which claims require real lot, installation or operating evidence. The study should explain why the selected arrangement can deliver the user's accepted material, not merely show a plausible tank drawing or a low unit-price comparison.

**Continue:** [Defend one complete chemical supply from origin to use and recovery](A-complete-qualified-chemical-supply-system.lingua#r_44MR9J6NH9MF50YCHKGAT4GMK3).

